f I want someone to fall in  love with my book I gotta fall in love  with it so that takes just a lot of work  well let's talk a little bit about the  book so Lola is the main character and  she is Island born but she can't  remember the island right yeah I think a  lot of us a lot of us can't remember our  origins  one of the things that happens and we're  surrounded by them we hear our parents  talking all the time about places they  grew up around or events that happened  before we could remember we grow up with  grandparents who often bring an entirely  different world  we're shaped by places and people that  we've never ever met and that's  something important to recognize our  origins are a part of our identity so  this is about identity formation about  from places you were from how does that  process take place for a keep for an  older person but also for then a little  kid I think that we tell each other  stories I think all of us when we think  about our grandparents if you have the  fortune to grow up around your  grandparents you through gainer you're  lucky enough you remember how gentle  they are how caring the are but you also  remember their stories it seemed to come  from another planet and stories bind us  across time and across space we have to  point out the illustrations will show  some of them while you're talking but  one of my favorite lines in the book -  Lola she says just because her  grandmother says just because you don't  remember place doesn't mean it's not in  you  you never name the island specifically  and you never and there's a monster of  course which there's always a good  monster in a book because with monsters  come heroes you never name the island  and you never name the monster why I  think it's important to leave space for  people to play and for people to project  their own imaginations and their own  experiences also my goddaughters were  raised both in Puerto Rico and the  Dominican Republic so I want to make  sure that 